Z||000025||dnixon||11-17-1999||03:24 AM||||Yeah, I agree that the taxes on gas suck.   I heard a program on the radio tonight where some guy had done a survey of several US and Canadian gas prices.   He found that before taxes and allowing for exchange rates and different gallon sizes, prices were still about 2/3 as high in the US as in Canada.   Also, he found the variation in price in any one town was 2 or 3 times higher in the US than in Canada.   I was in the UK a couple of months ago and found it about 2 to 3 times more expensive than here in Canada.   (Incidentally, when you post here, why don't you say where you're from.   It adds meaning to your messages.)<P>I just filled my 87GT with 87 octane gas.   I have found it runs better on that than the higher octanes, which gummed up the works with their additives and cause misfiring and stalling.<P>It cost me $CAN 0.564 a litre.   There are about 4.54l per Imperial gal, 3.63l per US gal, so that's about $US1.39 per US gal.   Could be worse, and nothing like what it is in Europe.||||reg||12
Z||000026||olympic||11-17-1999||02:14 PM||||I read a report that said that the octane in fuel starts to drop after about 2 weeks in the gas stations tanks!!  They conducted tests and found that the octane in the premium fuel was lower than the regular unleaded. The reason being that so few people buy premium that is can sit in the tanks for many weeks.  I burn regular unleaded in my Yamaha SRX snowmobile and add an octane booster like 104+. ||||reg||1
